<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A cable runs straight from the top of a mast at <m>A({-5},\,{-4},\,{4})</m> to an anchor at <m>B({-14},\,{-7},\,{7})</m> on a site in Kitui; coordinates are in metres. A marker P divides AB internally in the ratio <m>{1} : {2}</m>.</p><div>(a) <m>\overrightarrow{AP} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>(b) The position vector of P, <m>\overrightarrow{OP} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Go the right fraction of the way along AB, starting from A. <m>\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -9 \\ -3 \\ 3 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(a) AP is <m>{1}</m> parts out of <m>{3}</m>, so <m>\overrightarrow{AP} = \dfrac{ {1} }{ {3} }\,\overrightarrow{AB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{OP} = \overrightarrow{OA} + \overrightarrow{AP} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -5 \\ -4 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)} + {\left(\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -8 \\ -5 \\ 5 \end{array}\right)}</m>, so P is <m>({-8},\,{-5},\,{5})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -8 \\ -5 \\ 5 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>